IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc29-xxvii-b-information-trial.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART XXVII Summary Convictions, sections 788 to 809:
-- information, application of other Parts, jurisdiction, the trial, adjudication, memo of conviction, dismissal and costs.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- THE FORM OF A DUTY. Where the text says a person or court "shall" do something, the decision function is named "... is required to ..."
-- and answers whether the requirement bites on the facts (JUST TRUE); it does not report whether someone complied, because the text says
-- nothing about the consequence of non-compliance. The performance of a duty by a named party is a regulative rule, run with #TRACE
-- in ccc29-tests-xxvii-b.l4. Where the text opens a duty with "Where" or "When" and the opening fails, the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling (b)
-- of 2026-11-05); where the duty is addressed to a scope without such a word (for example "proceedings to which this Part applies") and
-- the case is outside the scope, the answer is NOTHING (ruling (c)). A power named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of
-- 2026-11-12); one whose gate is "where", "when", "on ..." or a time ("before or during") answers JUST FALSE and is listed in NOTES.md for a lawyer.

§ `Part XXVII -- Summary Convictions: information, trial and adjudication`

§§ `Section 788 -- Commencement of proceedings`

-- 788(1) Proceedings under this Part shall be commenced by laying an information in Form 2.
-- src:16722 | Commencement of proceedings
-- src:16723 | 788 (1) Proceedings under this Part shall be commenced by laying an information in Form 2.
@ref Criminal Code s 788(1) (src:16722-16723)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part, by s 785 proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 788(1) the proceedings are required to be commenced by laying an information in Form 2` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part, by s 785 proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proceedings under this Part shall be commenced"

DECLARE `s 788 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 788 lay an information in Form 2`

@ref Criminal Code s 788(1) (src:16722-16723)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 788 action`
`s 788(1) the informant is to lay an information in Form 2` MEANS
    PARTY `the informant`
    MUST `s 788 lay an information in Form 2`

-- 788(2) Notwithstanding any other law that requires an information to be laid before or to be tried by two or more justices, one justice may (a) receive the information; (b) issue a summons or warrant with respect to the information; and (c) do all other things preliminary to the trial.
-- src:16724 | One justice may act before the trial
-- src:16725 | (2) Notwithstanding any other law that requires an information to be laid before or to be tried by two or more justices, one justice may
-- src:16726 | (a) receive the information;
-- src:16727 | (b) issue a summons or warrant with respect to the information; and
-- src:16728 | (c) do all other things preliminary to the trial.
@ref Criminal Code s 788(2) to s 788(2)(c) (src:16724-16728)
DECLARE `s 788(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 788(2)(a) receive the information`
    `s 788(2)(b) issue a summons or warrant with respect to the information`
    `s 788(2)(c) do all other things preliminary to the trial`
    `s 788(2) an act at or after the trial`

@ref Criminal Code s 788(2) (src:16724-16725)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside the three acts
GIVEN act IS A `s 788(2) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 788(2) one justice may do the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 788(2)(a) receive the information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 788(2)(b) issue a summons or warrant with respect to the information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 788(2)(c) do all other things preliminary to the trial` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 788(2) an act at or after the trial` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do all other things preliminary to the trial"

§§ `Section 789 -- Formalities of information`

-- 789(1) In proceedings to which this Part applies, an information (a) shall be in writing and under oath; and (b) may charge more than one offence ... but where more than one offence is charged ..., each offence or matter of complaint ... shall be set out in a separate count.
-- src:16729 | Formalities of information
-- src:16730 | 789 (1) In proceedings to which this Part applies, an information
-- src:16731 | (a) shall be in writing and under oath; and
-- src:16732 | (b) may charge more than one offence or relate to more than one matter of complaint, but where more than one offence is charged or the information relates to more than one matter of complaint, each offence or matter of complaint, as the case may be, shall be set out in a separate count.
@ref Criminal Code s 789(1) to s 789(1)(b) (src:16729-16732)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 789(1)(a) the information is required to be in writing and under oath` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings to which this Part applies"

@ref Criminal Code s 789(1)(b) (src:16732)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside the scope
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 789(1)(b) the information may charge more than one offence or relate to more than one matter of complaint` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings to which this Part applies"

@ref Criminal Code s 789(1)(b) (src:16732)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `more than one offence is charged or the information relates to more than one matter of complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 789(1)(b) each offence or matter of complaint is required to be set out in a separate count` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings to which this Part applies"
        IF `more than one offence is charged or the information relates to more than one matter of complaint` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but where more than one offence is charged or the information relates to more than one matter of complaint"

