@ref Criminal Code s 790(2) (src:16737-16738)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-790-2); answers JUST FALSE when "Where" or "thereafter" fails
GIVEN `two or more justices have jurisdiction with respect to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial has been held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790(2) one justice may do anything required or authorized to be done in connection with the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `two or more justices have jurisdiction with respect to the proceedings` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where two or more justices have jurisdiction with respect to proceedings"
        IF NOT `the trial has been held` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "one justice may thereafter do anything"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 794 -- No need to negative exception`

-- 794(1) No exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification prescribed by law is required to be set out or negatived, as the case may be, in an information.
-- src:16745 | No need to negative exception, etc.
-- src:16746 | 794 (1) No exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification prescribed by law is required to be set out or negatived, as the case may be, in an information.
@ref Criminal Code s 794(1) (src:16745-16746)
GIVEN `it is an exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification prescribed by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 794(1) the information need not set out or negative the exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification` MEANS
    IF `it is an exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification prescribed by law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification prescribed by law"

§§ `Section 795 -- Application of Parts XVI, XVIII, XVIII.1, XX, XX.1 and XXII.01`

-- 795 The provisions of Parts XVI and XVIII with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice, the provisions of Parts XVIII.1, XX and XX.1, insofar as they are not inconsistent with this Part, and the provisions of Part XXII.01, apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part.
-- src:16750 | Application of Parts XVI, XVIII, XVIII.1, XX, XX.1 and XXII.01
-- src:16751 | 795 The provisions of Parts XVI and XVIII with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice, the provisions of Parts XVIII.1, XX and XX.1, insofar as they are not inconsistent with this Part, and the provisions of Part XXII.01, apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 795 (src:16750-16751)
DECLARE `s 795 Part of the Code` IS ONE OF
    `s 795 Part XVI`
    `s 795 Part XVIII`
    `s 795 Part XVIII.1`
    `s 795 Part XX`
    `s 795 Part XX.1`
    `s 795 Part XXII.01`
    `s 795 another Part`

@ref Criminal Code s 795 (src:16750-16751)
GIVEN part IS A `s 795 Part of the Code`
      `the provisions are with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions are inconsistent with Part XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `s 795 Part XVI` THEN `s 795 compelling appearance` `the provisions are with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice`
    WHEN `s 795 Part XVIII` THEN `s 795 compelling appearance` `the provisions are with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice`
    WHEN `s 795 Part XVIII.1` THEN `s 795 not inconsistent` `the provisions are inconsistent with Part XXVII`
    WHEN `s 795 Part XX` THEN `s 795 not inconsistent` `the provisions are inconsistent with Part XXVII`
    WHEN `s 795 Part XX.1` THEN `s 795 not inconsistent` `the provisions are inconsistent with Part XXVII`
    WHEN `s 795 Part XXII.01` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 795 another Part` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The provisions of Parts XVI and XVIII"

@ref Criminal Code s 795 (src:16750-16751)
GIVEN `the provisions are with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 795 compelling appearance` MEANS
    IF `the provisions are with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice"

@ref Criminal Code s 795 (src:16750-16751)
GIVEN `the provisions are inconsistent with Part XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 795 not inconsistent` MEANS
    IF `the provisions are inconsistent with Part XXVII`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "insofar as they are not inconsistent with this Part"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Sections 798 to 803 -- Trial: jurisdiction, appearances, arraignment, adjournment`

-- 798 Every summary conviction court has jurisdiction to try, determine and adjudge proceedings to which this Part applies in the territorial division over which the person who constitutes that court has jurisdiction.
-- src:16755 | Jurisdiction
-- src:16756 | 798 Every summary conviction court has jurisdiction to try, determine and adjudge proceedings to which this Part applies in the territorial division over which the person who constitutes that court has jurisdiction.
@ref Criminal Code s 798 (src:16755-16756)
GIVEN `the court is a summary conviction court, by s 785 summary conviction court` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in the territorial division over which the person who constitutes that court has jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798 the summary conviction court has jurisdiction to try, determine and adjudge the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the court is a summary conviction court, by s 785 summary conviction court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies`
       AND `the proceedings are in the territorial division over which the person who constitutes that court has jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the territorial division over which the person who constitutes that court has jurisdiction"

-- 799 Where ... the defendant appears for the trial and the prosecutor, having had due notice, does not appear, the summary conviction court may dismiss the information or may adjourn the trial to some other time on such terms as it considers proper.
-- src:16757 | Non-appearance of prosecutor
-- src:16758 | 799 Where, in proceedings to which this Part applies, the defendant appears for the trial and the prosecutor, having had due notice, does not appear, the summary conviction court may dismiss the information or may adjourn the trial to some other time on such terms as it considers proper.
@ref Criminal Code s 799 (src:16757-16758)
DECLARE `s 799 course` IS ONE OF
    `s 799 dismiss the information`
    `s 799 adjourn the trial to some other time on such terms as it considers proper`
    `s 799 another course`

@ref Criminal Code s 799 (src:16757-16758)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-799); answers JUST FALSE when "Where ... does not appear" fails
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant appears for the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor had due notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor does not appear` IS A BOOLEAN
      course IS A `s 799 course`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 799 the summary conviction court may take the course` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Part applies`
       AND `the defendant appears for the trial`
       AND `the prosecutor had due notice`
       AND `the prosecutor does not appear`
    THEN CONSIDER course
         WHEN `s 799 dismiss the information` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 799 adjourn the trial to some other time on such terms as it considers proper` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 799 another course` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may dismiss the information or may adjourn the trial"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in proceedings to which this Part applies, the defendant appears for the trial and the prosecutor, having had due notice, does not appear"

-- 800(1) Where the prosecutor and defendant appear for the trial, the summary conviction court shall proceed to hold the trial.
-- src:16759 | When both parties appear
-- src:16760 | 800 (1) Where the prosecutor and defendant appear for the trial, the summary conviction court shall proceed to hold the trial.
@ref Criminal Code s 800(1) (src:16759-16760)
GIVEN `the prosecutor and the defendant appear for the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
