§§ `Sections 804 to 809 -- Adjudication, memo of conviction, dismissal and costs`

-- 804 When the summary conviction court has heard the prosecutor, defendant and witnesses, it shall, after considering the matter, convict the defendant, discharge the defendant under section 730, make an order against the defendant or dismiss the information, as the case may be.
-- src:16801 | Finding of guilt, conviction, order or dismissal
-- src:16802 | 804 When the summary conviction court has heard the prosecutor, defendant and witnesses, it shall, after considering the matter, convict the defendant, discharge the defendant under section 730, make an order against the defendant or dismiss the information, as the case may be.
@ref Criminal Code s 804 (src:16801-16802)
GIVEN `the court has heard the prosecutor, defendant and witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 804 the summary conviction court is required to convict the defendant, discharge the defendant under section 730, make an order against the defendant or dismiss the information` MEANS
    IF `the court has heard the prosecutor, defendant and witnesses`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the summary conviction court has heard the prosecutor, defendant and witnesses"

DECLARE `s 804 decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 804 convict the defendant`
    `s 804 discharge the defendant under section 730`
    `s 804 make an order against the defendant`
    `s 804 dismiss the information`

DECLARE `s 804 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 804 the court decides` HAS decision IS A `s 804 decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 804 (src:16801-16802)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 804 action`
`s 804 the court is to decide` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 804 the court decides` decision

-- 806(1) If a defendant is convicted or an order is made in relation to the defendant, a minute or memorandum of the conviction or order must be made by the summary conviction court indicating that the matter was dealt with under this Part and, on request by the defendant, the prosecutor or any other person, a conviction or order in Form 35 or 36, as the case may be, and a certified copy ... must be drawn up and the certified copy must be delivered to the person making the request.
-- src:16804 | Memo of conviction or order
-- src:16805 | 806 (1) If a defendant is convicted or an order is made in relation to the defendant, a minute or memorandum of the conviction or order must be made by the summary conviction court indicating that the matter was dealt with under this Part and, on request by the defendant, the prosecutor or any other person, a conviction or order in Form 35 or 36, as the case may be, and a certified copy of the conviction or order must be drawn up and the certified copy must be delivered to the person making the request.
@ref Criminal Code s 806(1) (src:16804-16805)
GIVEN `the defendant is convicted or an order is made in relation to the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 806(1) a minute or memorandum indicating that the matter was dealt with under this Part is required to be made by the summary conviction court` MEANS
    IF `the defendant is convicted or an order is made in relation to the defendant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a defendant is convicted or an order is made in relation to the defendant"

DECLARE `s 806(1) form` IS ONE OF
    `s 806(1) Form 35, a conviction`
    `s 806(1) Form 36, an order`

@ref Criminal Code s 806(1) (src:16804-16805)
GIVEN `the defendant is convicted or an order is made in relation to the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a request is made by the defendant, the prosecutor or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 806(1) a conviction or order in Form 35 or 36 and a certified copy are required to be drawn up and the certified copy delivered to the person making the request` MEANS
    IF `the defendant is convicted or an order is made in relation to the defendant` AND `a request is made by the defendant, the prosecutor or any other person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a defendant is convicted or an order is made in relation to the defendant"

@ref Criminal Code s 806(1) (src:16804-16805)
GIVEN `it is a conviction rather than an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 806(1) form`
`s 806(1) the form to be drawn up` MEANS
    IF `it is a conviction rather than an order`
    THEN `s 806(1) Form 35, a conviction`
    ELSE `s 806(1) Form 36, an order`

-- 806(2) Where a defendant is convicted or an order is made against him, the summary conviction court shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 or 22, and section 528 applies in respect of a warrant of committal issued under this subsection.
-- src:16806 | Warrant of committal
-- src:16807 | (2) Where a defendant is convicted or an order is made against him, the summary conviction court shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 or 22, and section 528 applies in respect of a warrant of committal issued under this subsection.
