    IF `the warrant of committal is one issued under subsection 806(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a warrant of committal issued under this subsection"

-- 806(3) If a warrant of committal in Form 21 is signed by a clerk of a court, a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk, is admissible in evidence in any proceeding.
-- src:16808 | Admissibility of certified copy
-- src:16809 | (3) If a warrant of committal in Form 21 is signed by a clerk of a court, a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk, is admissible in evidence in any proceeding.
@ref Criminal Code s 806(3) (src:16808-16809)
GIVEN `the warrant of committal is in Form 21` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by a clerk of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is certified by the clerk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 806(3) the copy of the warrant of committal is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the warrant of committal is in Form 21` AND `it is signed by a clerk of a court` AND `the copy is certified by the clerk`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a warrant of committal in Form 21 is signed by a clerk of a court"

-- 807 Where several persons join in committing the same offence and on conviction each is adjudged to pay an amount to a person aggrieved, no more shall be paid to that person than an amount equal to the value of the property destroyed or injured or the amount of the injury done, together with costs, if any, and the residue of the amount adjudged to be paid shall be applied in the manner in which other penalties imposed by law are directed to be applied.
-- src:16810 | Disposal of penalties when joint offenders
-- src:16811 | 807 Where several persons join in committing the same offence and on conviction each is adjudged to pay an amount to a person aggrieved, no more shall be paid to that person than an amount equal to the value of the property destroyed or injured or the amount of the injury done, together with costs, if any, and the residue of the amount adjudged to be paid shall be applied in the manner in which other penalties imposed by law are directed to be applied.
@ref Criminal Code s 807 (src:16810-16811)
GIVEN `several persons join in committing the same offence and on conviction each is adjudged to pay an amount to a person aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the property destroyed or injured or the amount of the injury done` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs, if any` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 807 the most that is to be paid to the person aggrieved` MEANS
    IF `several persons join in committing the same offence and on conviction each is adjudged to pay an amount to a person aggrieved`
    THEN JUST (`the value of the property destroyed or injured or the amount of the injury done` PLUS `the costs, if any`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where several persons join in committing the same offence and on conviction each is adjudged to pay an amount to a person aggrieved"

@ref Criminal Code s 807 (src:16810-16811)
GIVEN `several persons join in committing the same offence and on conviction each is adjudged to pay an amount to a person aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total of the amounts adjudged to be paid to the person aggrieved` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the property destroyed or injured or the amount of the injury done` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs, if any` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 807 the residue to be applied in the manner in which other penalties imposed by law are directed to be applied` MEANS
    IF `several persons join in committing the same offence and on conviction each is adjudged to pay an amount to a person aggrieved`
    THEN IF `the total of the amounts adjudged to be paid to the person aggrieved` AT MOST (`the value of the property destroyed or injured or the amount of the injury done` PLUS `the costs, if any`)
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE JUST (`the total of the amounts adjudged to be paid to the person aggrieved` MINUS (`the value of the property destroyed or injured or the amount of the injury done` PLUS `the costs, if any`))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where several persons join in committing the same offence and on conviction each is adjudged to pay an amount to a person aggrieved"

-- 808(1) Where the summary conviction court dismisses an information, it may, if requested by the defendant, draw up an order of dismissal and shall give to the defendant a certified copy of the order of dismissal.
