    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the summary conviction court dismisses an information` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the summary conviction court dismisses an information"
        IF NOT `the defendant requests an order of dismissal` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it may, if requested by the defendant, draw up an order of dismissal"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 808(1) (src:16812-16813)
GIVEN `the court has drawn up an order of dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(1) the summary conviction court is required to give the defendant a certified copy of the order of dismissal` MEANS
    IF `the court has drawn up an order of dismissal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall give to the defendant a certified copy of the order of dismissal"

-- 808(2) A copy of an order of dismissal, certified in accordance with subsection (1) is, without further proof, a bar to any subsequent proceedings against the defendant in respect of the same cause.
