    IF `the copy of the order of dismissal is certified in accordance with subsection (1)` AND `the subsequent proceedings are against the defendant in respect of the same cause`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "certified in accordance with subsection (1)" and "in respect of the same cause"

-- 809(1) The summary conviction court may in its discretion award and order such costs as it considers reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840 as may be taken or allowed ..., to be paid (a) to the informant by the defendant, where the summary conviction court convicts or makes an order against the defendant; or (b) to the defendant by the informant, where the summary conviction court dismisses an information.
-- src:16816 | Costs
-- src:16817 | 809 (1) The summary conviction court may in its discretion award and order such costs as it considers reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840 as may be taken or allowed in proceedings before that summary conviction court, to be paid
-- src:16818 | (a) to the informant by the defendant, where the summary conviction court convicts or makes an order against the defendant; or
-- src:16819 | (b) to the defendant by the informant, where the summary conviction court dismisses an information.
@ref Criminal Code s 809(1) to s 809(1)(b) (src:16816-16819)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-809-1); answers JUST FALSE when "where the summary conviction court convicts" fails; NOTHING when the costs are not ones it considers reasonable (limit in its own wording)
GIVEN `the summary conviction court convicts or makes an order against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considers the costs reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840 as may be taken or allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(1)(a) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the informant by the defendant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the summary conviction court convicts or makes an order against the defendant` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the summary conviction court convicts or makes an order against the defendant"
        IF NOT `it considers the costs reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840 as may be taken or allowed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such costs as it considers reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 809(1)(b) (src:16819)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-809-1); answers JUST FALSE when "where the summary conviction court dismisses an information" fails; NOTHING when the costs are not ones it considers reasonable (limit in its own wording)
GIVEN `the summary conviction court dismisses an information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considers the costs reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840 as may be taken or allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(1)(b) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the defendant by the informant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the summary conviction court dismisses an information` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the summary conviction court dismisses an information"
        IF NOT `it considers the costs reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840 as may be taken or allowed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such costs as it considers reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 809(2) An order under subsection (1) shall be set out in the conviction, order or order of dismissal, as the case may be.
-- src:16820 | Order set out
-- src:16821 | (2) An order under subsection (1) shall be set out in the conviction, order or order of dismissal, as the case may be.
@ref Criminal Code s 809(2) (src:16820-16821)
GIVEN `it is an order for costs under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(2) the order for costs is required to be set out in the conviction, order or order of dismissal` MEANS
    IF `it is an order for costs under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order under subsection (1)"

-- 809(3) Where a fine or sum of money or both are adjudged to be paid by a defendant and a term of imprisonment in default of payment is imposed, the defendant is, in default of payment, liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed, and for the purposes of this subsection, any costs that are awarded against the defendant shall be deemed to be part of the fine or sum of money adjudged to be paid.
-- src:16822 | Costs are part of fine
-- src:16823 | (3) Where a fine or sum of money or both are adjudged to be paid by a defendant and a term of imprisonment in default of payment is imposed, the defendant is, in default of payment, liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed, and for the purposes of this subsection, any costs that are awarded against the defendant shall be deemed to be part of the fine or sum of money adjudged to be paid.
@ref Criminal Code s 809(3) (src:16822-16823)
GIVEN `a fine or sum of money or both are adjudged to be paid by the defendant and a term of imprisonment in default of payment is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine or sum of money adjudged to be paid, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs awarded against the defendant, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 809(3) the amount for which the defendant is liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed in default of payment` MEANS
    IF `a fine or sum of money or both are adjudged to be paid by the defendant and a term of imprisonment in default of payment is imposed`
    THEN JUST (`the fine or sum of money adjudged to be paid, in dollars` PLUS `the costs awarded against the defendant, in dollars`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a fine or sum of money or both are adjudged to be paid by a defendant and a term of imprisonment in default of payment is imposed"

-- 809(4) Where no fine or sum of money is adjudged to be paid by a defendant, but costs are awarded against the defendant or informant, the person who is liable to pay them is, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month.
-- src:16824 | Where no fine imposed
-- src:16825 | (4) Where no fine or sum of money is adjudged to be paid by a defendant, but costs are awarded against the defendant or informant, the person who is liable to pay them is, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month.
@ref Criminal Code s 809(4) (src:16824-16825)
GIVEN `no fine or sum of money is adjudged to be paid by a defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `costs are awarded against the defendant or the informant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(4) the person who is liable to pay the costs is, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month` MEANS
    IF `no fine or sum of money is adjudged to be paid by a defendant` AND `costs are awarded against the defendant or the informant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where no fine or sum of money is adjudged to be paid by a defendant, but costs are awarded against the defendant or informant"

@ref Criminal Code s 809(4) (src:16824-16825)
GIVETH A `Length of time`
`s 809(4) the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the costs` MEANS
    `Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE

-- 809(5) In this section, costs includes the costs and charges, after they have been ascertained, of committing and conveying to prison the person against whom costs have been awarded.
-- src:16826 | Definition of costs
-- src:16827 | (5) In this section, costs includes the costs and charges, after they have been ascertained, of committing and conveying to prison the person against whom costs have been awarded.
@ref Criminal Code s 809(5) "costs" (src:16826-16827)
GIVEN `they are costs awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are the costs and charges, after they have been ascertained, of committing and conveying to prison the person against whom costs have been awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(5) costs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `they are costs awarded` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `they are the costs and charges, after they have been ascertained, of committing and conveying to prison the person against whom costs have been awarded` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "costs includes the costs and charges"
